# Textus Knowledge Workbench CML Model

> NOTE FOR CODEX
>
> This is the canonical CML source location for the Workbench application model.
> Replace this scaffold with valid current CML after inspecting Cozy/CML grammar and representative src/main/cozy/*.cml files.
> Do not invent unsupported syntax.
>
> Design sources:
> - docs/notes/architecture.md
> - docs/journal/2026-09-23-knowledge-workbench-establishment.md
> - docs/phase/phase-1.md
>
> Primary application use case:
> - Form and approve knowledge from a raw Knowledge Candidate.
>
> Model Use Case and Application Workflow separately where supported.
>
> Phase 1 workflow:
> Register Candidate
> -> Resolve Evidence / Context
> -> Edit / Correct
> -> Semantic Grounding / Mapping
> -> Compose KnowledgeFormationProposal
> -> Human Review
> -> Approve / Hold / Reject
> -> Submit approved proposal to KnowledgeHub Knowledge Formation
> -> retain Formation Trace.
>
> Candidate sources:
> - TKL PreparedMaterial / raw candidate
> - NICT Editing Studio capture-derived candidate
>
> Important boundaries:
> - TKW owns candidate lifecycle and human formation/approval.
> - TKL owns evidence federation/preparation.
> - Editing Studio owns publishing/editorial domain interaction and views.
> - KnowledgeHub owns Knowledge processing/runtime/formation/storage.
> - Reuse CNCF/KnowledgeHub canonical types where semantics match.
>
